VENDORED. Under pact/vendor/ are copies of code the contract depends on, kept only so the test
suite can load the dependencies the contract compiles against:

  * fixtures/coin.pact, fixtures/fungible-v2.pact, fixtures/fungible-xchain-v1.pact —
    Kadena's coin contract (a test fixture of it) and fungible interfaces. Not ours.
  * block-history.pact — the block record the contract reads. Ours: Smart Pacts publishes it
    separately, under its own licence, at github.com/SmartPacts/block-history.

They are not part of the deployed artifact. On chain the contract resolves the real modules by
name, and pins the block record by hash.
